id: pm-gh1074
title: "GH-1074: package doctor cannot distinguish a safe declining service override from a global interceptor"
description: "GitHub issue #1074 reports that strict isolated package doctor fails a package whose output_format service always returns the documented handled:false decline decision, even though runtime behavior is inert and warning-free."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:packages",github,sdk,service-ownership
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:42:05.594Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:50.987Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:50.379Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:50.379Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Add an SDK-declared service ownership or safe-pass-through contract; keep global interception fail-closed; align doctor diagnostics with the runtime handled:false decision; test third-party package, first-party collision, and negative interceptor controls; document author guidance."
parent: pm-tnud
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Install a package that registers output_format and always returns handled:false; verify native output is unchanged; run package doctor --project --isolated --strict-exit; observe extension_output_service_override_global and exit 1."
resolution: "Resolved: service overrides can declare strictly validated pass-through ownership that runtime and package doctor enforce without masking real interceptors."
expected_result: Doctor retains warnings for genuine interceptors but recognizes declared ownership or a machine-verifiable unconditional decline.
actual_result: A safe canonical decline is classified as a global interceptor and fails strict doctor.
affected_version: 2026.8.21
component: package doctor
